+The CLI's HTTP transport is shared by pairing, reconciliation, usage upload, source disconnect, and
+installation revoke. It preserves request methods, headers, and bodies, refuses redirects, times
+out requests after 15 seconds, validates response bodies through the protocol module, and retries
+only transient failures. `Retry-After` is honored for rate limits and server errors but capped at
+five minutes (or the bounded test override); otherwise retries use capped exponential backoff with
+small jitter. The prepared runtime includes this transport module so installed hooks and CLI copies
+use the same behavior as the source checkout.
